From 5784b98adf33cada104933144d107b4b8c1a1817 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 23:03:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] perf(dsv41): pack compressor BF16 weights to 12-bit
 selectively

Upstream base: 19f2c20ed4d64ae22bd009ceacadd85e2a81e354.
Immediate base: a75357bba81e31e4f3085700f94b6a0b29aed44a.

Pack DeepSeek-V4.1 compressor BF16 projections (TileLangSplitLinearMethod:
compressor.fused_wkv_wgate at ratio 2 and ratio 1) losslessly into 12-bit
storage (pack_bf16_weight) while keeping L2-hot/prefetched router.gate
([384, 5120], TileLangLinearMethod) and indexer.weights_proj ([32, 5120],
TileLangScaledLinearMethod) in uncompressed BF16.

Add prologue exception-range binary search (vllm_packed_bf16_filter_exc with
a zero-read fast path when num_exceptions == 0), SWAR __byte_perm 16-element
unpacking (vllm_packed_bf16_decode_vec16) with STACK:0 register usage,
warp-per-row coalesced packed_bf16_unpack for large prefill, occupancy-aware
pipeline staging across TP1/TP3/TP4..TP8 compressor shard shapes (N in {1024,
512, 384, 256, 192, 128, 64}, K = 5120), and split-K routing up to M = 256
(M = 512 for N <= 128) within the existing workspace budget.

Quality: 100% lossless bit-exact reconstruction and identical FP32 shard
accumulation order (0 ULP drift across all batch sizes and shard shapes,
including subnormal/out-of-window CSR exceptions).

Tests: 22 GPU tests pass in tests/kernels/quantization/test_deepseek_v41_tilelang_linear.py
(test_split_linear, test_packed_bf16_compressor_shapes_exact, test_bf16_gemm)
and 2-boot GB10 benchmarks across all 8 compressor shapes verify 0 ULP drift
and STACK:0 on all 68 compiled cubins.
Upstream status: local DeepSeek-V4.1 TileLang kernel optimization.
